# warpdrive.script — rules evaluated top-to-bottom each tick (first match wins).
# Conditions: in "Room" | has-stat-points | mob "Name" | hp-below N | hp-above N | always
# Actions:    train str con dex | goto "Room" | kill "Mob" | retreat "Room" |
#             rest | retreat-rest "Room" | say "text" | look
#
# $tokens below are substituted from client.yaml / CLI flags at load time:
#   $mob        -> mob: / --mob          (the target mob to kill)
#   $mob_room   -> mob_room: / --mob-room (the room that mob lives in)
#   $home       -> home: / --home        (rest / retreat destination; default Town Square)
#   $rest_hp    -> rest_hp: / --rest-hp  (rest until HP reaches this percent; default 95)
#   $retreat_hp -> retreat_hp: / --retreat-hp (retreat home to heal below this; default 50)
# Edit those in client.yaml instead of touching this file.
#
# Order matters: put the survival rules FIRST so they override fighting.

# 1) If we're in the mob room and HP has dropped to the retreat threshold,
#    haul back to Town Square and heal. Placed AFTER the kill rule so we keep
#    fighting while the mob is actually present, but once it's dead (or we're
#    just hurt) we go home instead of grinding into single digits.
when hp-below $retreat_hp do retreat-rest "$home"

# 2) While resting at home with low HP, keep resting until the rest_hp threshold
#    (set via --rest-hp / 'rest_hp:' in client.yaml, default 95) so we don't
#    march back to the mob half-healed. The server's `rest` heals ~12%/sec.
when in "$home" and hp-below $rest_hp do rest

# 3) Train stats whenever we're home and have points banked.
when in "$home" and has-stat-points do train str con dex

# 4) Fight the target mob if it's here.
when mob "$mob" do kill "$mob"

# Otherwise head to the mob's room (BFS over the discovered map).
when always do goto "$mob_room"
